  "summary": "Artistic practice that considers the internet as a given condition rather than a tool or virtual space",
  "description": "Explores the relationship between digital and physical worlds, often using internet aesthetics and themes in physical art forms. It reflects on how digital experiences shape contemporary reality.",
  "culturalContext": "Post-Internet art — Marisa Olson's term (2008), artists as Gene McHugh's blog chronicled (Agathe Snow, Petra Cortright, Ryan Trecartin, Jon Rafman) — treats the internet as ambient condition, not medium: screenshots as canvases, browser aesthetics in galleries, \"advanced laziness\", and art that lives equally as JPEG and object. 2014-era market boom (Vdrome, Evergold, (post)internet surveys) passed; the style's URL-to-IRL translation grammar remains the visual language of contemporary digital-native art.",
